{
  "rolesVersion": 2,
  "revision": "rev2 — 2026-07-27. Corrects all three signal-driven rules after the MP-7 signal audit: `recipe.course` did not exist; `usda.foodCategory` was the wrong field name with the wrong 25-value vocabulary; `dravya.classification` supplied Sanskrit keys with zero overlap with the data. All three are now bound to real fields with their real vocabularies, read directly from the repo. rev1 context follows.  Written after MP-6b produced culinarily absurd plans that passed all 23 hard properties: infant formula served to adults three times in one week, a breakfast of four chocolate drinks, and a dinner of six dried herbs beside raw lentils. Nothing in the catalogue said what a row IS FOR. This file says it.",
  "author": "Director",
  "appliesTo": "Every row of the 14,484-item FoodItem catalogue, plus the 1,500 authored recipes. Consumed by the MP-5 solver as an eligibility and composition constraint, and by properties C1-C9 of plan-validity-properties.json as their vocabulary.",
  "whyThisExists": "minAgeMonths is a FLOOR, not a range. Infant formula carries a floor of 0 and therefore satisfies every adult age check in the system. The catalogue can express 'not before this age' and cannot express 'intended for infants, inappropriate for adults'. It also cannot express 'this is a seasoning, not a dish'. Both failures produced the same symptom in MP-6b. A role is the missing field.",
  "matching": {
    "reuse": "Reuse the food-concepts.json rev5 matcher — same normalization, same contiguous token-sequence phrase match, same order-independent vetoTokens, same suffix negation, token-boundary only and NEVER substring. Do not write a second matcher.",
    "pluralTolerance": {
      "spec": "A phrase token matches a catalogue token when they are identical, or differ by a trailing 's', or by a trailing 'es', or by y->ies, or appear together in irregularPlurals below. Case-folded.",
      "irregularPlurals": {
        "leaf": "leaves",
        "loaf": "loaves",
        "knife": "knives",
        "half": "halves",
        "roti": "rotis",
        "dal": "dals"
      },
      "FC1_DEFECT": "food-concepts.json rev5 specifies trailing-'s' ONLY. That rule does not match 'potatoes' from 'potato', 'tomatoes' from 'tomato', 'berries' from 'berry', or 'leaves' from 'leaf'. It was caught here by running this file's own goldens against its own rules: 'Potatoes, flesh and skin, raw' — the exact row that produced the FC-1 `flesh` defect — resolved to `other`. The same fix must be applied to food-concepts.json and its 117 exclusion goldens re-run. Tracked as FC-1f in TASK-MP7.md."
    }
  },
  "resolution": {
    "algorithm": "Evaluate EVERY rule against the row. Collect all that match. Take the highest `priority`. Break ties by longest matched phrase in tokens; break remaining ties by the order rules appear in this file. A rule with `vetoTokens` or `vetoPhrases` that fires is discarded before priority is considered.",
    "priorityBands": {
      "100": "explicit per-row overrides",
      "95": "exclusionary detectors (infant, supplement, non-food)",
      "85": "authored recipe course — real data, outranks every name guess",
      "82": "narrow corrections to the 80 band",
      "80": "name phrases strong enough to override the USDA category",
      "70": "USDA foodCategory map",
      "62": "medicinal dravyas",
      "60": "general name phrases",
      "40": "dravya classification fallback",
      "0": "default `other`"
    },
    "default": "other",
    "singleAssignment": "Exactly one role per row. Unlike food-concepts.json, roles are not a set and do not roll up a hierarchy."
  },
